  "lineage": "1930s-1940s American jazz orchestra format with sectional brass-and-reed arrangement, 14-18 musicians, and dance-band repertoire emphasis. The Swing Era dominated American popular music c.1935-1945, with Benny Goodman, Count Basie, Duke Ellington, Glenn Miller, Tommy Dorsey, and Artie Shaw orchestras as canonical bandleaders. Distinguished from earlier hot-jazz by swing big band's formal-arranged composition (vs improvisational-collective) framework and dance-floor commercial-orientation.",
